# Paperless-ngx — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/paperless.sops.json.

# Django
# Paperless does NOT crash without it — it falls back to the literal default in
# the public repo, making every session cookie forgeable. openssl rand -hex 32
PAPERLESS_SECRET_KEY=changeme_hex32

# Superuser
# Read once, at the initial migration. Single-token username on purpose.
# openssl rand -base64 24
PAPERLESS_ADMIN_USER=admin
PAPERLESS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme_strong_password

# Postgres
# Same value twice: the postgres image initialises the role with
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD, paperless connects with PAPERLESS_DBPASS. initdb applies
# it on FIRST start only — to rotate on an existing cluster, change both keys
# then: docker exec -it paperless_db psql -U paperless \
#   -c "ALTER USER paperless PASSWORD '<new>';"
# (Both were the literal `paperless` in compose until 2026-08-31 — an older
# cluster still has that on disk.) openssl rand -hex 24
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme_hex24

